### Database requirements

- UUID primary keys.
- Foreign key constraints.
- Appropriate indexes.
- Unique constraints.
- Timestamps.
- Updated-at triggers.
- Database transactions for multi-step operations where necessary.
- RLS policies.
- Proper cascade behaviour.
- Admin role authorization.

### Important relationships

- One season has many participating teams.
- One player can have many season records.
- One season has one configurable rule set.
- One user can own multiple squads.
- One squad belongs to one season and one selected franchise.
- One squad contains many players.
- One squad has one or more saved Playing XI configurations, if supported by the product design.
- One squad can have a share record.
- One squad can have a rating snapshot.

Prevent duplicate player selections using a unique constraint on squad_id and player_id.

Keep player ratings and statistics separate from player master records.

Do not store multiple player IDs as an unstructured comma-separated string.

